# Base64 golden vectors.
#
# Two alphabets are pinned (NET-11.3):
#   std     -> RFC 4648 standard ('+' '/', '=' padding)
#   urlsafe -> RFC 4648 url-safe ('-' '_', '=' padding)
#
# Format (fields '|'-separated):
#   <name> | <input-spec> | <std-encoded> | <urlsafe-encoded>
#
# <input-spec> uses the same grammar as the SHA vectors. An empty
# encoded field is written as the literal token <EMPTY> to keep the
# column count stable.
#
# The RFC 4648 §10 progressive-length vectors ("", f, fo, foo, foob,
# fooba, foobar) exercise every padding length (0, 1, 2 '=' chars).
# The high-byte vectors prove the alphabet divergence: std emits
# '+' '/', url-safe emits '-' '_'.
empty   | empty            | <EMPTY>   | <EMPTY>
f       | ascii:f          | Zg==      | Zg==
fo      | ascii:fo         | Zm8=      | Zm8=
foo     | ascii:foo        | Zm9v      | Zm9v
foob    | ascii:foob       | Zm9vYg==  | Zm9vYg==
fooba   | ascii:fooba      | Zm9vYmE=  | Zm9vYmE=
foobar  | ascii:foobar     | Zm9vYmFy  | Zm9vYmFy
hi-bytes| hex:fbffbf       | +/+/      | -_-_
plusslash| hex:fb          | +w==      | -w==
